<script>
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={[
        '/middleware/middleware',
        '/middleware/signed-in',
        '/middleware/require-role',
        '/reactive/is-failed',
    ]}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/guards.test.ts',
            from: ["test('readOnly refuses a write ReadOnly at 403"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/guards.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('readOnly hands a read and a write to an allowed handler to next",
            ],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Archive last year's pipeline for reading">
        <p>File the rung with <code>middleware</code> in a layout, and every request below that
            route is covered. A <code>GET</code>, <code>HEAD</code> or <code>OPTIONS</code>
            passes, and any other method is refused <code>ReadOnly</code> at 403.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script server>
            import { middleware, readOnly } from '@abide/abide/server'

            middleware(readOnly({ message: 'Last year’s pipeline is archived.' }))
            </script>

            <slot />
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Keep sign-in open on a demo that takes no changes">
        <p>List the handlers whose writes stay open in <code>allow</code>. Each is matched by its
            address, so a renamed file is still matched.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script server>
            import { middleware, readOnly } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import signIn from './account/signIn.handler.ts'
            import signOut from './account/signOut.handler.ts'

            middleware(readOnly({ allow: [signIn, signOut] }))
            </script>

            <slot />
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Read the ReadOnly refusal on a write">
        <p>Filed in a layout, the refusal is not one of the handler's typed failures. Check it
            with <code>isFailed</code>.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="browser" code={`
            import { isFailed, reactive } from '@abide/abide'
            import reopenDeal from './reopenDeal.handler.ts'

            const notice = reactive('')
            try {
                await reopenDeal()
            } catch (refusal) {
                if (!isFailed(refusal)) throw refusal
                notice.set(\`\${refusal.status} \${refusal.message}\`)
            }
        `} />
    </Section>
</Doc>
